WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.600
Hi, welcome back to the Lam Rim,

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.950
and I bet you're wondering what the holes

00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:07.640
in these jeans are, and let's find out.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.700
I'm going to go to the text now.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:13.350
We finished the terrible
and wonderful story

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:16.008
of the Lady of the Blue Lotus, Utpala,

00:00:16.008 --> 00:00:18.325
who became an arhat

00:00:18.325 --> 00:00:21.850
and who made 500 arhats out of her nuns.

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:25.630
Here we continue with Pabongka Rinpoche's

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:26.875
Lam Rim lecture.

00:00:26.875 --> 00:00:30.510
'DAS ZIN PAS NA MA MIN PAR MI 'GYUR TE

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:35.270
Just because your mom was in the past,

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:37.970
doesn't mean she's not your mom.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:42.970
Just because the days of being
your mom were in the past,

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:47.077
doesn't mean she's not your mom.

00:00:47.077 --> 00:00:49.827
DE 'GYUR NA TSE STOD
KYI MA YANG TSE SMAD KYI

00:00:49.827 --> 00:00:51.110
MA MIN PAR 'GYUR

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:56.110
Then logically, if the
fact that she's passed,

00:00:56.370 --> 00:01:00.430
if the fact that the time she's
been your mother is passed,

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.290
means she's not your mother,

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:05.510
then everybody's mother
is not their mother,

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:08.750
because everybody's mother
was their mother before,

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:09.970
in this life.

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:13.830
So that means, if your mom
is not your mother this year,

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:15.910
she was your mother last year,

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:17.290
then she's not your mother, right?

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:19.950
According to your logic,

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:23.140
if she's been your mother in the past,

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:25.110
she's not your mother now.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:27.990
Okay, well, then the mom who
gave you birth in this life

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:29.280
is not your mom.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.210
Because she gave you birth before.

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:34.434
This is Pabongka's argument.

00:01:34.434 --> 00:01:38.133
KHA SANG GI MA YANG DE
RING GI MA MIN PAR 'GYUR TE

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:40.990
Even your mom from yesterday
wouldn't be your mom today,

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:42.760
because that's passed.

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:46.530
So if you went to visit
your mother yesterday,

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:48.870
then you came home today, then suddenly,

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:51.150
because the day changed,

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:52.760
she's not your mother anymore, right?

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:54.970
Because someone in the past
has been your mother, is

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:58.566
not your mother, according
to your logic. Why?

00:01:58.566 --> 00:02:00.610
DE 'DAS ZIN PAS SO

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:02.560
Because it's passed, she's passed.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:05.075
Yesterday is also passed.

00:02:06.398 --> 00:02:08.210
'DI NI PHRA BA'I MI RTAG PA STE

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:09.739
This is interesting, he says,

00:02:09.739 --> 00:02:12.386
"That's a kind of subtle impermanence."

00:02:12.386 --> 00:02:14.626
PHRA BA means subtle,

00:02:14.626 --> 00:02:16.300
MI RTAG PA means impermanent.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:19.380
THOS PA MA BYAS PAS RTOGS PAR DKA' MOD

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:22.470
If you haven't had a Buddhist education,

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:25.970
with the Lam Rim or with the ACI courses,

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:29.860
then RTOGS PAR DKA'
it's difficult to grasp.

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:35.670
Subtle impermanence is difficult to grasp

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:38.300
if you are not trained formally.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:41.130
If you haven't had
formal Buddhist training,

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:42.365
training in the classics,

00:02:42.365 --> 00:02:44.020
Mixed Nuts Classics,

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:46.037
then it's going to be difficult,

00:02:46.037 --> 00:02:48.673
RTOGS DKA' difficult to catch it.

00:02:48.673 --> 00:02:51.041
MOD means look, I know

00:02:51.041 --> 00:02:53.810
but let's try to take
it to a common example

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:56.286
and I think it will be
easier for you guys.

00:02:56.286 --> 00:02:58.285
DPER NA let's take an example.

00:02:58.285 --> 00:02:59.652
GZAN 'DI LTA BU

00:02:59.652 --> 00:03:01.740
So of course Pabongka Rinpoche

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:05.210
is giving his Lam Rim lecture,

00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:06.269
with a GZAN.

00:03:06.269 --> 00:03:08.410
GZAN means the shawl

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:12.130
that the monks wear over their shoulders.

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:14.150
So he would have been giving his lecture

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:16.787
with his shawl over his shoulders.

00:03:16.787 --> 00:03:19.838
'DI LTA BU YANG NA NING

00:03:19.838 --> 00:03:21.340
So NA NING means last year,

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:22.636
it's an idiom.

00:03:22.636 --> 00:03:24.221
NA NING means last year.

00:03:24.221 --> 00:03:26.970
GSAR PA'I SKABS NA NING

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:31.387
Last year, this shawl I have
on my shoulders was new.

00:03:32.464 --> 00:03:35.488
GSAR PA'I SKABS DRI MA CAN MIN

00:03:35.488 --> 00:03:38.179
It wasn't stinky.

00:03:38.179 --> 00:03:41.940
And you know, to be honest,
people use their shawl

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:45.680
for everything in the monastery.
So it does get kind of,

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:50.680
and I have known monks,
I lived with a monk

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:55.640
who said it was unhealthy to
take a shower in the winter.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:59.050
So he wouldn't take a shower all winter.

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:01.300
He wouldn't wash his body all winter,

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:04.030
and so it does get kind of DRI MA CAN,

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:08.070
means 'mala', right?

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:10.358
It has a good smell.

00:04:10.358 --> 00:04:13.440
BUG RDOL means get holes in it,

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:15.340
like holes in your jeans.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:16.840
We have BUG RDOL,

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:19.150
the best example of BUG RDOL

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.610
in our culture, modern culture, is jeans,

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:23.240
the holes in your jeans.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:27.350
So look, these jeans didn't
have these holes a year ago,

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:30.840
but this year they have holes.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:35.000
So he says, "Look at
this shawl I have on."

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.830
Geshe Michael could say, "Look
at these jeans I have on."

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:39.440
You know, BUG RDOL,

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:41.340
they have holes in them.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:44.100
But they didn't have
holes in them last year.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:47.340
Did they? And they
weren't smelly last year.

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:49.231
But now they're smelly.

00:04:49.231 --> 00:04:50.064
BUG RDOL YANG MED PA LA

00:04:50.064 --> 00:04:53.330
DE'I RGYUN DENG SANG
GI GZAN 'DI DRI MA CAN

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:55.670
But you can't say these are not the jeans

00:04:55.670 --> 00:05:00.353
that I bought last year.
It's a very profound proof.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:04.170
It's a very profound way of teaching

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.995
us subtle impermanence.

00:05:06.995 --> 00:05:09.635
- Look, do you have jeans on? - Yes.

00:05:09.635 --> 00:05:11.752
- Do they have holes in them? - Yes.

00:05:11.752 --> 00:05:14.262
- Did they have holes
in them last year? - No.

00:05:14.262 --> 00:05:15.887
- Are they the same jeans?

00:05:15.887 --> 00:05:19.430
- Well yeah, they're the
same jeans, they're my jeans.

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:21.170
So he says, "There you go,

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:24.850
now you understand subtle
impermanence, got it?"

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:27.790
But you cannot say that the jeans today

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:30.200
that have holes in them are not the jeans

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:33.046
that you bought at...what's that store?

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:36.230
Buckle, last year.

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:37.960
They are the jeans you bought last year.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.640
They are the same jeans.

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:43.557
Why are we talking about that here?

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:47.250
Yeah, your mom's changed, she's different.

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:48.290
Maybe she's BUG RDOL,

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:51.567
maybe she's got a hole somewhere,

00:05:51.567 --> 00:05:53.410
but it's still the same mom.

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:55.110
You can't say it's not the same mom.

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:57.780
Just because she looks
older or she's not around,

00:05:57.780 --> 00:05:58.790
or something, you can't say

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:00.660
it's not the same mom. Come on.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:03.885
It's the same jeans, right? It's logic.

00:06:03.885 --> 00:06:04.793
BUG RDOL YANG MED PA LA

00:06:04.793 --> 00:06:07.500
DE'I RGYUN DENG SANG
GI GZAN 'DI DRI MA CAN.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:11.050
We're talking about the
flow of an object over time,

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:12.880
it's called RGYUN.

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:16.244
And the flow of your mom over time.

00:06:16.244 --> 00:06:18.744
DRI MA CAN, BUG RAL CAN DU 'DUG PAS,

00:06:18.744 --> 00:06:19.919
DE GNYIS THA DAD PA LTA BU YIN,

00:06:19.919 --> 00:06:21.620
Are they separate,

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:24.044
or are they not separate, or are they one?

00:06:24.044 --> 00:06:27.520
Are they two points on a stream,

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.500
or are they two unconnected things?

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:32.800
Is there a pair of jeans
last year that was new

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:35.270
from the store, and then
there is a pair of jeans

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:37.210
this year that has holes in it?

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:38.530
- Are they separate? - Yes.

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:40.810
- Are they connected by a stream? - Yes.

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:42.680
- Are they still the same jeans? - Yes.

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:45.710
- Is it still your mom? - Yes.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:49.327
DE LTA NA'ANG SKYE BA SNGA
PHYI'I MA GNYIS KYIS AA MA

00:06:49.327 --> 00:06:51.135
BYAS PA LA KHYAD MED DU BSAM

00:06:51.135 --> 00:06:54.751
You got to follow

00:06:54.751 --> 00:06:58.180
this train of thought until you realize

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:02.090
that there's no difference
between your mom in this life,

00:07:02.090 --> 00:07:05.160
which is the jeans with the holes in them,

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:09.420
and the mom in your last life,
which is the new jeans, okay?

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:13.528
Your mom in your last
life is the new jeans,

00:07:13.528 --> 00:07:16.192
and your mom in this life is the jeans,

00:07:16.192 --> 00:07:17.250
the mom with the holes in it.

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:20.730
And they are one stream. It's one thing.

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:23.140
If they were your mom in this life,

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:25.200
and they were your mom in a previous life,

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:27.420
it's the same person.
It's the same person.

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.182
It's the same jeans.

00:07:29.182 --> 00:07:31.007
KHYAD MED DU BSAM DGOS TE

00:07:31.007 --> 00:07:32.824
You got to think about it.

00:07:32.824 --> 00:07:35.982
NA NING SROG BSKYABS NA
DE'I DRIN DA LO YANG DRAN

00:07:35.982 --> 00:07:37.390
DGOS PA BZHIN NO

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:38.770
I love this sentence.

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:39.603
I don't know why,

00:07:39.603 --> 00:07:41.049
but this sentence has always stuck with me

00:07:41.049 --> 00:07:43.817
over many years.

00:07:43.817 --> 00:07:45.800
NA NING SROG BSKYABS

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:47.770
If someone saves your life,

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:52.770
in 2020. Maybe in 2021 you
can show some gratitude.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:58.700
Okay? 2020 someone pulls you off

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.280
from an automobile accident or something,

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:04.170
saves your life. What? In
2021, you're going to say,

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:06.440
oh, that was last year.

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:10.570
This is 2021, I don't have
to be grateful anymore.

00:08:10.570 --> 00:08:13.616
"Come on", he says.

00:08:13.616 --> 00:08:17.232
DE LTAR YANG YANG SBYANGS
PAS MAR SHES RGYUD LA

00:08:17.232 --> 00:08:18.557
SKYES PA'I TSAD NI

00:08:18.557 --> 00:08:19.981
This is very beautiful.

00:08:19.981 --> 00:08:22.760
TSAD means how do you know

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:24.151
when you got it.

00:08:24.151 --> 00:08:25.910
TSAD means measure, right?

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:29.450
Like TSAD MA. Like pramana.

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:33.573
How do you know when you've reached

00:08:33.573 --> 00:08:35.660
MAR SHES?

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:40.660
Which is kind of 1.5 of
the, how many?, 5 point...

00:08:42.136 --> 00:08:43.728
RGYU 'BRAS MAN NGAG BDUN

00:08:43.728 --> 00:08:46.180
7 points of how to get bodhicitta.

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:49.454
It's really 1.5. What's 1.0?

00:08:50.374 --> 00:08:52.814
1.0 is equanimity.

00:08:52.814 --> 00:08:56.314
1.5 is, it's kind of like a 1.5,

00:08:57.400 --> 00:08:59.140
to realize they've been your mother.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:02.840
So how do you know? And I love that in the

00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:06.390
Buddhist scripture when
they say, with an emotion,

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:08.840
how do you know when you got it.

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:10.580
When can you say,

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:11.900
I have MAR SHES?

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:13.040
At what point can you say,

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:14.203
I have MAR SHES?

00:09:14.203 --> 00:09:16.844
When can you say RGYUD LA SKYES?

00:09:16.844 --> 00:09:19.427
RGYUD LA SKYES means I have got
that realization in my mind.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:23.450
I really do think of everyone as my mom.

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:24.631
How do you know?

00:09:24.631 --> 00:09:28.160
SEMS CAN GROG SBUR GCIG MTHONG BA NA'ANG

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:31.070
Even if you just see a
single ant crawling across

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:33.760
the bathroom downstairs in the building,

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:36.321
which used to happen.

00:09:36.321 --> 00:09:37.746
SEMS CAN GROG SBUR GCIG MTHONG

00:09:37.746 --> 00:09:38.587
especially when

00:09:38.587 --> 00:09:41.559
you are sitting and
meditating in the bathroom,

00:09:41.559 --> 00:09:43.647
you see an ant crawling around.

00:09:43.647 --> 00:09:48.647
MTHONG BA NA'ANG RANG DE'I BUR GYUR SKABS

00:09:48.855 --> 00:09:50.876
There was a time

00:09:50.876 --> 00:09:53.735
when I was this being's child.

00:09:53.735 --> 00:09:56.090
When you see an ant crawling on the floor

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:58.600
of the bathroom and you're
sitting there meditating,

00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:03.600
and you automatically think,
I was once this ant's child.

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:09.895
I was once the baby of this ant.

00:10:09.895 --> 00:10:12.938
SKYID SDUG TSANG MA DE LA RE DOGS

00:10:12.938 --> 00:10:17.205
Misspelled in the original
text, very subtle.

00:10:17.205 --> 00:10:21.160
RE DOGS means all my hopes and fears

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:23.180
depended on this person.

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:26.150
Whether I was going to have
a good day or a bad day,

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:28.780
whether I was going to
survive today or not,

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:30.120
depended on this person.

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:32.370
So, if you're sitting in the bathroom

00:10:32.370 --> 00:10:34.630
and you see an ant
crawling across the floor,

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:38.343
and you think, there was a
day when I was her child,

00:10:38.343 --> 00:10:43.313
and my very life depended
on her from hour to hour.

00:10:43.313 --> 00:10:45.096
BYUNG BA LHANG LHANG

00:10:45.096 --> 00:10:48.812
means... what do you call it? un-evoked?

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:53.370
I don't know, LHANG LHANG means

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:56.870
when that comes up in your heart uncalled?

00:10:58.305 --> 00:11:03.230
Yeah just totally spontaneously.
You're not thinking

00:11:03.230 --> 00:11:05.920
I should feel compassion or
I should feel this emotion,

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:08.417
but just the emotion
takes over your heart.

00:11:08.417 --> 00:11:10.100
LHANG LHANG, like that.

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:13.410
Oh wow, this is the one
that I was looking for

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:16.102
to survive the day, this bug.

00:11:16.102 --> 00:11:18.670
MAR SHES RGYUD LA BYUNG BA

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:20.510
then you've got MAR SHES.

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:25.292
And he uses the honorific word for born,

00:11:25.292 --> 00:11:28.015
'KHRUNGS PA is SKYE PA.

00:11:29.562 --> 00:11:34.512
It's a very telling verb choice.

00:11:35.990 --> 00:11:40.990
He says thou hast given
birth in your holy heart to

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:43.530
MAR SHES.

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:46.870
He's using the high honorific
that we would use to a Buddha.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:50.250
It means if you could get to that point,

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:52.010
where you had this emotion about

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:54.970
a single ant crawling across the floor,

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:59.000
then you're really a high practitioner.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:02.980
JO BO RJE LTA BU DGOS TSUL BCAS GSUNGS

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:06.001
You guys have to be like Atisha,

00:12:06.001 --> 00:12:07.510
like Lord Atisha.

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:10.430
This is how he would feel about an ant.

00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:12.230
When you can feel about an ant

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:13.640
the way that Atisha

00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:17.090
would feel about an ant, automatically,

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:18.650
despite yourself,

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:21.780
then you have MAR SHES.

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:24.630
So I guess we'll never get there.

00:12:24.630 --> 00:12:27.010
You got an ant picture for me?

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:29.910
This is, I found this picture,

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:33.510
this little girl playing with ants.

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:35.840
I guess you must have
done that. I did that.

00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:39.431
We used to kill them
actually, which is really bad.

00:12:39.431 --> 00:12:43.113
But she's playing with ants.

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:47.478
Maybe she's having those thoughts.

00:12:47.478 --> 00:12:50.080
With this, we have reached 2.0.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:52.660
We have reached the
second of the seven steps

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:55.270
for developing bodhicitta.

00:12:55.270 --> 00:12:56.510
And that's called DRIN DRAN

00:12:56.510 --> 00:12:58.509
Say DRIN DRAN

00:12:58.509 --> 00:13:01.468
It's not Ting Ting, it's DRIN DRAN

00:13:01.468 --> 00:13:04.940
DRIN DRAN means to recall the kindness.

00:13:04.940 --> 00:13:07.516
BKA' DRIN DRAN PA

00:13:07.516 --> 00:13:10.380
BKA' DRIN means kindness,

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:12.660
DRAN PA means to remember.

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:15.498
DRIN DRAN is the short word.

00:13:15.498 --> 00:13:16.350
DRIN DRAN

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:19.600
Second step. Don't forget
what we're talking about.

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:24.250
We're talking about actually
six steps you can do

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:25.770
to reach a seventh result,

00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:27.330
which is bodhicitta.

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:30.270
Supposedly, if you just go through

00:13:30.270 --> 00:13:32.360
these steps one by one,

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:33.630
you'll get to bodhicitta

00:13:33.630 --> 00:13:36.670
without thinking about
it, which is really cool.

00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:38.347
That's the purpose of the Lam Rim.

00:13:38.347 --> 00:13:42.340
The Lam Rim means just do this meditation,

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:44.431
then do that meditation,
then do that meditation,

00:13:44.431 --> 00:13:47.070
and then, even if you don't
want to, you're going to be

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:49.583
a bodhisattva.

00:13:49.583 --> 00:13:52.441
DE LTAR SEMS CAN RNAMS
AA MA YIN PAR MNYAM NA,

00:13:52.441 --> 00:13:56.182
AA MA BYAS SKABS DRIN SHIN
TU CHE BAR BSAM DGOS PAS

00:13:56.182 --> 00:13:59.883
So I think all of us,
because of the old jeans,

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:03.140
we are closer to believing

00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:05.720
that everyone has been our mom before.

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:08.410
But how did she treat
us when she was our mom?

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:09.951
What did she do for us?

00:14:09.951 --> 00:14:11.784
So let's talk about that.

00:14:11.784 --> 00:14:14.760
Let's talk about DRIN SHIN TU CHE

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:17.010
SKABS DRIN SHIN TU CHE

00:14:17.010 --> 00:14:18.990
When she was our mom,
how did she treat us?

00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:20.070
Here we go.

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:22.887
DA LTA TSE 'DI'I MA 'DI LTA BUR MTSON NA

00:14:22.887 --> 00:14:27.000
MTSON hear means, it can mean weapon, like

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:30.391
MTSON CHA'I 'KHOR LO
-- The Crown of Knives,

00:14:31.433 --> 00:14:36.433
but MTSON can also mean
to take as an example.

00:14:36.433 --> 00:14:38.841
So here, it's to take as an example.

00:14:38.841 --> 00:14:41.810
Let's take as an example,
let's just talk about

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:44.284
the mom you had in this life.

00:14:44.284 --> 00:14:47.117
THOG MTHA' BAR GSUM DU DRIN CHE STE

00:14:47.117 --> 00:14:49.974
She has been kind to you.

00:14:49.974 --> 00:14:53.200
THOG MTHA' BAR -- This is a famous idiom.

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:56.087
Do you guys know THOG MTHA' BAR?

00:14:57.084 --> 00:14:58.919
Tsongkapa wrote a poem called

00:14:58.919 --> 00:15:00.268
THOG MTHA' BAR

00:15:00.268 --> 00:15:02.810
It means in the beginning,
in the end, and in-between.

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:04.650
In the beginning, in
the end, and in-between.

00:15:04.650 --> 00:15:09.013
So she has been extremely
kind to us in the beginning,

00:15:09.013 --> 00:15:12.959
in the end, and in all the time between.

00:15:12.959 --> 00:15:15.583
THOG MAR ZLA DGU NGO BCU

00:15:15.583 --> 00:15:18.374
What's the beginning?

00:15:18.374 --> 00:15:21.550
It's in the womb. She carried you for

00:15:21.550 --> 00:15:22.383
ZLA DGU

00:15:22.383 --> 00:15:25.030
nine months.

00:15:25.030 --> 00:15:26.367
Then he says NGO BCU,

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:30.610
which means ten days.

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:32.680
Tibetans believed that normal term is

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:34.860
nine months and ten days.

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:36.353
Is it true? I don't know.

00:15:36.353 --> 00:15:38.520
(unclear)

00:15:40.423 --> 00:15:42.164
TBAR LUS LA KHUR BA

00:15:42.164 --> 00:15:43.406
There's KHUR BA again, Tim.

00:15:43.406 --> 00:15:45.600
She bore that burden.

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:48.543
She carried that burden for
nine months and ten days.

00:15:48.543 --> 00:15:50.909
BU LA GNOD KYIS DOGS NAS

00:15:50.909 --> 00:15:54.630
This DOGS means suspicion.

00:15:54.630 --> 00:15:57.246
And here it means

00:15:58.150 --> 00:16:01.230
worried that something
might happen to her child.

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:04.027
Worried that something
might happen to her child.

00:16:04.027 --> 00:16:07.642
RANG NYID KYIS ZAS SKOM
'GRO 'DUG THAMS CAD GZAB

00:16:07.642 --> 00:16:10.212
GZAB GZAB in modern Tibetan,

00:16:10.212 --> 00:16:13.039
GZAB GZAB means be super careful.

00:16:13.039 --> 00:16:14.580
GZAB GZAB BYED

00:16:14.580 --> 00:16:15.930
Like if someone is

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:20.070
I don't know, using a sharp
knife to cut something,

00:16:20.070 --> 00:16:21.686
the mom might say GZAB GZAB

00:16:21.686 --> 00:16:23.045
GZAB GZAB BYED

00:16:23.045 --> 00:16:26.721
Be careful. Here it means

00:16:26.721 --> 00:16:29.157
Just deciding ZAS

00:16:29.157 --> 00:16:30.948
Just deciding SKOM

00:16:30.948 --> 00:16:33.081
Just deciding 'GRO

00:16:33.081 --> 00:16:34.630
Just deciding 'DUG

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:35.830
She would GZAB GZAB

00:16:35.830 --> 00:16:40.313
She would try to proceed
with great caution about,

00:16:41.375 --> 00:16:45.003
ZAS means what she eats,

00:16:45.003 --> 00:16:47.195
SKOM means what she drinks,

00:16:47.195 --> 00:16:51.092
'GRO means the manner
in which she walks, and

00:16:51.092 --> 00:16:53.405
'DUG means the manner in which she sits.

00:16:53.405 --> 00:16:58.380
So she would be cautious
about even what she drank

00:16:59.878 --> 00:17:02.660
because she would be thinking,
how will it affect my child?

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:04.160
How will it affect my child?

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:08.160
If I walk quickly, will it hurt the child?

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:10.680
If I sit in a certain way,
will that hurt the child?

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:14.080
She's always thinking of the child.

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:16.200
Intense caring.

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:18.742
I got a picture here for you.

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:24.319
On a good day, I guess,
all of us who are pregnant

00:17:24.319 --> 00:17:28.020
would decide to eat the salad,

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:33.020
just for the baby, even though salads are

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:35.062
an anathema,

00:17:36.770 --> 00:17:39.320
are terrible.

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:41.640
She would eat a salad just for the baby.

00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:43.300
She's not thinking about herself.

00:17:43.300 --> 00:17:45.509
She's thinking about the baby.

00:17:45.509 --> 00:17:48.743
DE'I TSE MAS DE LTAR
BSKYANGS MKHAS PA ZHIG

00:17:48.743 --> 00:17:50.801
MA BYUNG PHYIN

00:17:50.801 --> 00:17:51.792
This is a difficult sentence.

00:17:51.792 --> 00:17:53.100
DE'I TSE means

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:55.053
if in those pregnant days,

00:17:55.933 --> 00:17:57.352
MAS is instrumental.

00:17:57.352 --> 00:17:59.735
If my mom

00:17:59.735 --> 00:18:00.874
DE LTAR BSKYANGS means

00:18:00.874 --> 00:18:05.874
to sustain a certain behavior

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:08.996
If she had not been a MKHAS PA

00:18:08.996 --> 00:18:11.775
What's a MKHAS PA?

00:18:11.775 --> 00:18:16.213
Like Kedrup Tenpa Dargye, Kedrup Je,

00:18:17.899 --> 00:18:20.650
Yeah, like a master. If
she had not been a master

00:18:20.650 --> 00:18:22.290
in deciding what to eat and drink

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:24.160
and how to walk and how to sit,

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:27.680
if she had not been a
master of considering

00:18:27.680 --> 00:18:31.092
her child's welfare,

00:18:31.092 --> 00:18:34.490
MA BYUNG PHYIN means in that eventuality,

00:18:34.490 --> 00:18:37.200
In that case, MA BYUNG PHYIN

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:42.200
if she had not been so
mindful about what to eat,

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:45.060
what to do, then you and I wouldn't be

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:47.293
in the Lam Rim right now.

00:18:47.293 --> 00:18:49.030
It's a very beautiful sentence.

00:18:49.030 --> 00:18:51.660
You and I wouldn't be here
listening to the Lam Rim.

00:18:51.660 --> 00:18:55.290
We would have died. We would be retarded,

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:59.480
or we wouldn't have made it here

00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:03.020
if she had not taken those care

00:19:03.020 --> 00:19:05.380
before we came out.

00:19:05.380 --> 00:19:10.380
So it's a very compelling
argument to a big bunch of monks.

00:19:10.730 --> 00:19:12.470
Here's a big bunch of monks

00:19:12.470 --> 00:19:15.560
who enjoy their Geshe classes,

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:18.100
and then Pabongka says,

00:19:18.100 --> 00:19:20.900
he doesn't say she saved
your life, bla bla bla.

00:19:20.900 --> 00:19:22.751
He says, "You wouldn't have studied

00:19:22.751 --> 00:19:24.820
Abhisamayalankara if it hadn't been

00:19:24.820 --> 00:19:25.653
for your mom."

00:19:25.653 --> 00:19:27.527
Oh my God, can you imagine?

00:19:27.527 --> 00:19:29.880
You wouldn't have ever heard of

00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:31.807
Middle Way.

00:19:31.807 --> 00:19:34.330
And then all the monks
are like, "Oh, my God".

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:39.066
Our moms are so cool.

00:19:39.066 --> 00:19:40.640
RANG RE DA LTA means

00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:43.593
all of us sitting here right now

00:19:43.593 --> 00:19:45.010
CHOS DANG MJAL

00:19:45.010 --> 00:19:45.843
This MJAL is

00:19:45.843 --> 00:19:50.020
a very important word
in Buddhist language.

00:19:50.020 --> 00:19:53.713
It means to encounter a holy thing.

00:19:54.930 --> 00:19:56.840
MJAL -- like when you,

00:19:56.840 --> 00:20:00.450
I remember people would come to see

00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:02.060
the Mongolian Temple where I lived.

00:20:02.060 --> 00:20:05.200
And they would come to
see the paintings mostly.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:09.019
I would tell my teacher, Rinpoche,

00:20:09.019 --> 00:20:10.960
I'd say, I'm going to go
show them the paintings.

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:15.000
He'd say, "No, no, no. We don't
say show them the paintings.

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:17.630
They are going to meet the Holy Dharma."

00:20:17.630 --> 00:20:19.960
You have to say CHOS DANG MJAL

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:21.509
Say CHOS DANG MJAL

00:20:21.509 --> 00:20:22.414
(students repeating)

00:20:22.414 --> 00:20:23.808
CHOS means dharma.

00:20:23.808 --> 00:20:25.830
DANG means with.

00:20:25.830 --> 00:20:27.060
MJAL means meet.

00:20:27.060 --> 00:20:28.400
Meet with the dharma.

00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:31.240
So you don't say, "I'm going
to go look at paintings."

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:33.515
You say, "I'm going to
go meet the Holy Dharma."

00:20:33.515 --> 00:20:36.240
It's a beautiful word.

00:20:36.240 --> 00:20:38.500
So you wouldn't have had the chance

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:40.560
to CHOS DANG MJAL if your mom

00:20:40.560 --> 00:20:43.290
hadn't been careful
drinking what she drank

00:20:43.290 --> 00:20:45.300
when you were in her womb.

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:47.716
DAM PA'I CHOS LA SLOB
TU YOD PA 'DI MI 'BYUNG

00:20:47.716 --> 00:20:51.007
AYou wouldn't be here today
studying the Holy Dharma

00:20:51.007 --> 00:20:53.750
if your mom had not taken great care,

00:20:53.750 --> 00:20:56.960
even in the womb, even in the womb.

00:20:56.960 --> 00:21:01.533
And for a person who really
values their dharma life,

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:06.840
then that's a very huge argument.

00:21:06.840 --> 00:21:10.670
That's a huge piece of logic.

00:21:10.670 --> 00:21:13.703
- You better be nice to your mom. - Why?

00:21:13.703 --> 00:21:17.250
- Because she's why you're
sitting in the Lam Rim right now.

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:19.630
Can you imagine not being
in the Lam Rim right now?

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:21.320
I know what I would be.

00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:24.449
I would be a professor at
Princeton or something.

00:21:24.449 --> 00:21:27.160
And I would be unhappy, and
I would have two divorces,

00:21:27.160 --> 00:21:30.117
and I'd be drinking wine every night

00:21:30.117 --> 00:21:33.910
to make my life a little more bearable and

00:21:33.910 --> 00:21:37.090
struggling against my colleagues to see

00:21:37.090 --> 00:21:39.960
who could publish a book
first. And I would be there.

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:44.293
I know. So, I'm grateful.

00:21:44.293 --> 00:21:48.251
T'DI DAG KYANG RANG NYID RGOD
DRAGS NAS BYUNG BA MIN GYI

00:21:48.251 --> 00:21:50.640
This is very funny because RGOD

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:55.131
this is the RGOD in BYING RGOD

00:21:55.131 --> 00:21:57.800
BYING BA and RGOD PA

00:21:57.800 --> 00:22:00.270
Meditation obstacles.

00:22:00.270 --> 00:22:03.330
Dullness and agitation.

00:22:03.330 --> 00:22:05.710
So this RGOD means agitation.

00:22:05.710 --> 00:22:07.910
What's the word for a chimpan-,

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:11.252
a large, what do you call it, chimpanzee?

00:22:11.252 --> 00:22:13.400
What's the large, smaller than an ape,

00:22:13.400 --> 00:22:15.770
bigger than a monkey?

00:22:15.770 --> 00:22:19.050
I'm sorry, smaller than a
gorilla, bigger than a monkey?

00:22:19.050 --> 00:22:20.167
Chimpanzee?

00:22:20.167 --> 00:22:21.619
[Student] Orangutang?

00:22:21.619 --> 00:22:23.350
[GMR] Yeah, orangutang.

00:22:23.350 --> 00:22:25.168
What's the Tibetan word for orangutang?

00:22:25.168 --> 00:22:28.180
MI RGOD

00:22:28.180 --> 00:22:29.430
Agitated human.

00:22:33.410 --> 00:22:36.568
So RGOD DRAGS

00:22:36.568 --> 00:22:38.330
This DRAGS with this RGOD means

00:22:38.330 --> 00:22:41.668
your effort and your cleverness.

00:22:41.668 --> 00:22:45.910
The fact that you're sitting
here in a dharma class,

00:22:45.910 --> 00:22:47.570
or in a Mixed Nuts class,

00:22:47.570 --> 00:22:50.090
with the holiest of dharma,

00:22:50.090 --> 00:22:52.920
was not because you were so clever

00:22:52.920 --> 00:22:55.180
or you were so, you were so sharp

00:22:55.180 --> 00:22:56.710
that you got yourself here.

00:22:56.710 --> 00:22:58.960
It's just that your mom
drank the right thing

00:22:58.960 --> 00:23:00.400
while she was pregnant.

00:23:00.400 --> 00:23:01.810
And if she had drunk something else,

00:23:01.810 --> 00:23:04.050
you wouldn't have had
the brains to sit here.

00:23:04.050 --> 00:23:06.829
And that's true, right, so...

00:23:06.829 --> 00:23:09.729
MIN GYI, AA MA DE NYID KYI DRIN

00:23:09.729 --> 00:23:10.903
It's only your mom.

00:23:10.903 --> 00:23:13.695
DE NYID means it's only,

00:23:13.695 --> 00:23:16.120
all the credit goes to your
mom that you have a brain

00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:19.970
to sit here in Lam Rim. Think about it.

00:23:19.970 --> 00:23:21.520
She could have taken drugs.

00:23:21.520 --> 00:23:22.640
She could have done other things.

00:23:22.640 --> 00:23:24.373
She could have drunk alcohol.

00:23:24.373 --> 00:23:29.373
You could be mentally
dull from her misbehavior

00:23:31.110 --> 00:23:33.050
while you were, while she was pregnant,

00:23:33.050 --> 00:23:34.940
but she took take of you even then.

00:23:34.940 --> 00:23:39.491
She started... When you think
about the mother's kindness,

00:23:39.491 --> 00:23:41.640
DRIN DRAN, step number 2,

00:23:41.640 --> 00:23:44.580
don't start with after your birth.

00:23:44.580 --> 00:23:46.510
Start from after your conception.

00:23:46.510 --> 00:23:48.533
She started taking care of you then.

00:23:48.533 --> 00:23:51.783
Probably even before conception, right?

00:23:54.590 --> 00:23:57.260
So I like this photo.

00:23:57.260 --> 00:23:59.740
When I think about... I
said, I'm going to go find

00:23:59.740 --> 00:24:03.420
a picture of a Lam Rim teaching
that we'd been through,

00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:08.030
so I can say that we were there.

00:24:08.030 --> 00:24:09.330
And I love this picture.

00:24:09.330 --> 00:24:11.220
This is a Lam Rim that we had in Bali,

00:24:11.220 --> 00:24:13.240
recently like a year ago.

00:24:13.240 --> 00:24:17.950
And this is the Vietnamese contingent.

00:24:17.950 --> 00:24:19.560
These are the students from Vietnam.

00:24:19.560 --> 00:24:20.720
They did a beautiful dance.

00:24:20.720 --> 00:24:23.190
Then the Japanese did a nice dance.

00:24:23.190 --> 00:24:25.792
And then the Chinese did a nice dance.

00:24:25.792 --> 00:24:30.792
And for us to stand there and
watch this beautiful dance

00:24:31.950 --> 00:24:33.883
in the middle of a highest teaching,

00:24:35.480 --> 00:24:39.940
you wouldn't be there if
your mom had abused her body

00:24:39.940 --> 00:24:41.130
while she was pregnant.

00:24:41.130 --> 00:24:45.353
She was taking care of
you before you came out.

00:24:45.353 --> 00:24:49.761
BAR DU SKYES PA NA'ANG
GANG YANG MI SHES PA

00:24:49.761 --> 00:24:50.676
Now, he says,

00:24:50.676 --> 00:24:54.217
BAR THOG MTHA' BAR

00:24:54.217 --> 00:24:56.725
THOG means in the beginning.

00:24:56.725 --> 00:24:58.980
MTHA' means at the end.

00:24:58.980 --> 00:25:01.370
BAR means in-between.

00:25:01.370 --> 00:25:03.211
Let's talk about BAR.

00:25:03.211 --> 00:25:05.580
BAR starts when you come out.

00:25:05.580 --> 00:25:10.499
The in-between starts after
your born from the womb.

00:25:10.499 --> 00:25:12.749
BAR DU SKYES PA NA'ANG

00:25:12.749 --> 00:25:14.090
Even after you were born,

00:25:14.090 --> 00:25:15.756
you are a

00:25:15.756 --> 00:25:19.490
GANG YANG MI SHES PA SHA'I 'BU

00:25:19.490 --> 00:25:23.090
You are a lump of stupid flesh

00:25:23.090 --> 00:25:24.650
that doesn't know anything.

00:25:24.650 --> 00:25:29.650
You are a ball of meat
that don't know nothing.

00:25:32.570 --> 00:25:33.727
That sounds like a good thing

00:25:33.727 --> 00:25:36.357
you can call people that upset you.

00:25:36.357 --> 00:25:39.370
You're just a ball of meat
who don't know nothing.

00:25:39.370 --> 00:25:41.480
I love this sentence, I don't know why.

00:25:41.480 --> 00:25:43.650
This sentence stays with me also.

00:25:43.650 --> 00:25:47.780
You were just a ball of stupid meat.

00:25:49.480 --> 00:25:51.360
SOR BCU'I means

00:25:51.360 --> 00:25:54.376
SOR here means fingers and

00:25:54.376 --> 00:25:57.388
SOR BCU'I RTZE LA BLANGS means to

00:25:58.690 --> 00:25:59.523
I don't know,

00:25:59.523 --> 00:26:02.190
to hold something up on
your fingers like that.

00:26:02.190 --> 00:26:06.803
She's laying. She just had
her guts ripped out by you,

00:26:08.120 --> 00:26:11.760
and she almost died,
and then she's got this

00:26:11.760 --> 00:26:14.710
little, stupid ball of meat.

00:26:14.710 --> 00:26:18.631
And she's like, "Oh, you're so beautiful."

00:26:18.631 --> 00:26:20.315
And she's like, holds you
up on her ten fingers.

00:26:20.315 --> 00:26:22.573
And I saw a picture of Nour

00:26:22.573 --> 00:26:25.660
like this a month ago. She's like,

00:26:25.660 --> 00:26:28.763
we were following the hospitals today.

00:26:29.630 --> 00:26:31.642
It's the usual drama:

00:26:31.642 --> 00:26:34.610
She went to the hospital. Her water broke.

00:26:34.610 --> 00:26:36.839
She went to hospital.
They race to the hospital.

00:26:36.839 --> 00:26:39.330
Okay, is it out yet? No, no, no.

00:26:39.330 --> 00:26:42.450
Then, you know, you do
your work. Have dinner.

00:26:42.450 --> 00:26:44.600
You call Seiji. -Is it out yet? - No.

00:26:44.600 --> 00:26:46.550
- She's screaming. -Okay I got it.

00:26:46.550 --> 00:26:51.080
And then you keep,

00:26:51.080 --> 00:26:52.343
sometimes you forget to call Seiji.

00:26:52.343 --> 00:26:55.431
Next morning you're
like, "I forgot to call

00:26:55.431 --> 00:26:56.725
Seiji last night."

00:26:56.725 --> 00:27:00.497
You call, say, "Is it out yet?"
- No, she's still screaming.

00:27:00.497 --> 00:27:03.170
And then suddenly your phone rings,

00:27:03.170 --> 00:27:04.850
and you got this photo

00:27:04.850 --> 00:27:06.230
of Nour with the baby

00:27:06.230 --> 00:27:10.130
like this. Ain't it the truth?

00:27:10.130 --> 00:27:11.737
It's always been like that.

00:27:11.737 --> 00:27:13.947
BAR DU

00:27:13.947 --> 00:27:15.814
SKYES PA NA'ANG

00:27:15.814 --> 00:27:17.312
She is SOR BCU'I RTZE LA BLANGS

00:27:17.312 --> 00:27:20.448
She's holding you on the tips
of her ten fingers. Then,

00:27:20.448 --> 00:27:23.015
RNYED PA LTA BU'I DGA' TSOR BYAS

00:27:23.015 --> 00:27:25.191
She looks blissed out
like she's just found

00:27:25.191 --> 00:27:28.956
a bag of diamonds.

00:27:28.956 --> 00:27:32.290
It's so funny. It's such
a funny picture to me.

00:27:32.290 --> 00:27:33.747
She's not saying,

00:27:33.747 --> 00:27:36.010
"You almost killed me two hours ago."

00:27:36.010 --> 00:27:39.590
She's like, "Oh, look at this
beautiful, precious thing."

00:27:39.590 --> 00:27:42.566
Like she found a new bag
of diamonds or something.

00:27:42.566 --> 00:27:47.566
She's treating this ball of
stupid meat, ball of idiot meat,

00:27:49.210 --> 00:27:52.460
that would make a good name for a band,

00:27:54.000 --> 00:27:56.520
She's treating you like a
bag of diamonds or something.

00:27:56.520 --> 00:27:59.190
Oh look, I found a bag of diamonds.

00:27:59.190 --> 00:28:00.670
You can see these pictures.

00:28:00.670 --> 00:28:02.480
This is a universal picture.

00:28:02.480 --> 00:28:05.266
It's not hard to find this picture.

00:28:05.266 --> 00:28:07.024
BU DE SOR BCU'I RTZE LA BLANGS

00:28:07.024 --> 00:28:08.774
GTER RNYED PA LTA BU'I DGA' TSOR BYAS

00:28:08.774 --> 00:28:11.798
DGA' TSOR means she's blissed out.

00:28:11.798 --> 00:28:13.980
SHA'I DROD LA BCAR

00:28:13.980 --> 00:28:15.510
SHA'I DROD means the warmth of her body.

00:28:15.510 --> 00:28:18.770
This is one of the levels of SBYOR LAM.

00:28:19.617 --> 00:28:23.900
Was it? DROD RTZE MO CHOS MCHOG

00:28:26.476 --> 00:28:29.617
DROD, RTZE MO, BZOD PA, CHOS MCHOG

00:28:29.617 --> 00:28:32.130
So DROD means warmth.

00:28:32.130 --> 00:28:33.960
In philosophical terms also,

00:28:33.960 --> 00:28:37.260
getting close to an
emptiness is called warmth.

00:28:37.260 --> 00:28:40.290
Here, SHA'I DROD means her flesh.

00:28:40.290 --> 00:28:41.433
The warmth of her flesh.

00:28:41.433 --> 00:28:44.710
BCAR means she presses you

00:28:44.710 --> 00:28:47.530
to the warmth of her flesh.

00:28:47.530 --> 00:28:49.463
'JAM PA'I STAN LA BZHAG

00:28:49.463 --> 00:28:50.754
She tries to find

00:28:50.754 --> 00:28:53.448
places to put you which are 'JAM PA,

00:28:53.448 --> 00:28:55.831
like 'JAM PA'I DBYANGS

00:28:55.831 --> 00:28:57.740
What's the Sanskrit?

00:28:58.725 --> 00:29:00.450
Manju.

00:29:00.450 --> 00:29:03.027
And that's a common
name for women in India,

00:29:03.027 --> 00:29:03.860
Manju.

00:29:03.860 --> 00:29:06.892
Gentle or velvety, or something like that.

00:29:06.892 --> 00:29:08.890
So when she lays you down,

00:29:08.890 --> 00:29:11.075
she tries to find a
nice, soft place for you.

00:29:11.075 --> 00:29:13.150
A manju place for you.

00:29:13.150 --> 00:29:17.010
That's a good way to remember Manjushri.

00:29:17.010 --> 00:29:19.250
And then, BRTZE BA'I 'DZUM GYIS BSUS,

00:29:19.250 --> 00:29:20.583
this is the BSUS that
the Buddha did to Utpala

00:29:22.320 --> 00:29:24.786
when he first saw her,

00:29:26.660 --> 00:29:28.598
greeted, he greeted you.

00:29:28.598 --> 00:29:30.460
This BSUS means to greet.

00:29:30.460 --> 00:29:32.850
And she greets with you a BRTZE BA'I 'DZUM

00:29:32.850 --> 00:29:35.060
means a smile of total love.

00:29:35.060 --> 00:29:37.650
You just ripped my guts out.

00:29:37.650 --> 00:29:39.150
I was bleeding all over the place.

00:29:39.150 --> 00:29:40.760
They just sewed me up.

00:29:40.760 --> 00:29:42.820
The painkillers are wearing off.

00:29:42.820 --> 00:29:45.379
I love you. You're so beautiful.

00:29:45.379 --> 00:29:49.210
It's crazy, right?

00:29:50.408 --> 00:29:53.158
SNABS LAS PAS PHYI CHOG PA

00:29:53.158 --> 00:29:54.966
SNABS means snot

00:29:55.970 --> 00:29:59.863
that comes out of a kid's
nose. It is, I'm sorry.

00:30:01.850 --> 00:30:03.725
LAG PAS PHYI CHOG PA

00:30:03.725 --> 00:30:07.993
CHOG PA means to allow
or to be appropriate.

00:30:09.070 --> 00:30:12.840
Like when you ask your
teacher, can I leave now?

00:30:12.840 --> 00:30:15.602
You say 'GRO CHOG PA -- can I leave now?

00:30:15.602 --> 00:30:19.080
Can I, do you need me for anything else?

00:30:19.080 --> 00:30:21.160
This CHOG PA means she could have,

00:30:21.160 --> 00:30:25.752
it would have been okay if
she wiped your snot with her

00:30:25.752 --> 00:30:29.250
LAG PA, from your nose,

00:30:29.250 --> 00:30:32.136
with her hand, with her fingers. But,

00:30:32.136 --> 00:30:34.690
GNOD DOGS, this is the DOGS we just had.

00:30:34.690 --> 00:30:37.088
She's afraid it might
hurt you. So she wipes it

00:30:37.088 --> 00:30:40.300
with her KHA,

00:30:40.300 --> 00:30:41.133
[Student] Mouth.

00:30:41.133 --> 00:30:45.810
Yeah, she wipes the snot out
of your nose with her lips,

00:30:45.810 --> 00:30:49.510
because she's afraid her
fingers might be too rough.

00:30:50.693 --> 00:30:51.526
DOGS

00:30:51.526 --> 00:30:52.621
MI GTZANG BA

00:30:52.621 --> 00:30:54.586
Your poo poo,

00:30:54.586 --> 00:30:55.844
SHING LA SOGS PAS BRAD

00:30:55.844 --> 00:30:56.677
She could

00:30:56.677 --> 00:31:00.570
scrape it out with some
plastic spoon or something,

00:31:00.570 --> 00:31:03.000
but she uses her LAG PA,

00:31:03.000 --> 00:31:06.540
her hands, because she's
afraid it might irritate

00:31:06.540 --> 00:31:10.460
your bottom, like a spoon
or some kind of cloth

00:31:10.460 --> 00:31:14.102
or something, and she
uses her own fingers.

00:31:14.102 --> 00:31:17.343
PHYIS means to wipe.

00:31:19.297 --> 00:31:24.297
ZHABS PHYIS means, what's that mean?

00:31:29.150 --> 00:31:32.771
Shoe shiner -- ZHABS PHYIS.

00:31:32.771 --> 00:31:37.653
It's the Tibetan word
for a Lama's attendant.

00:31:37.653 --> 00:31:40.340
The polite Tibetan word
for Lama's attendant

00:31:40.340 --> 00:31:41.830
is ZHABS PHYIS.

00:31:41.830 --> 00:31:44.630
Wiper of the holy shoes.

00:31:44.630 --> 00:31:46.930
Hey Holy Shoe Wiper,

00:31:46.930 --> 00:31:48.930
what's Rinpoche want for dinner today?

00:31:48.930 --> 00:31:51.190
Or something like that.

00:31:51.190 --> 00:31:53.000
Okay Jigme?

00:31:54.089 --> 00:31:57.789
DE'I SKABS SU RANG NYI MA
GCIG GAM CHU TSOD GCIG TZAM

00:31:57.789 --> 00:32:00.710
RING YAL BAR DOR NA'ANG

00:32:00.710 --> 00:32:05.620
Now if she had decided to take a break

00:32:05.620 --> 00:32:09.557
and leave us alone for
a day, or even an hour.

00:32:09.557 --> 00:32:11.714
NYI MA GCIG means a day,

00:32:11.714 --> 00:32:13.580
GAM means or,

00:32:13.580 --> 00:32:15.040
CHU TSOD GCIG means one hour,

00:32:15.040 --> 00:32:18.640
if she had decided, you
know let me take a break,

00:32:18.640 --> 00:32:20.480
I'm going to go,

00:32:20.480 --> 00:32:21.830
go see a movie or something,

00:32:21.830 --> 00:32:24.158
in a theater.

00:32:24.158 --> 00:32:28.887
YAL BAR DOR means to leave you,

00:32:28.887 --> 00:32:33.887
YAL DOR means to abandon somebody.

00:32:34.670 --> 00:32:39.670
If she had left me for a day,
24 hours, or even one hour,

00:32:40.190 --> 00:32:41.620
and gone to see a movie,

00:32:41.620 --> 00:32:45.225
or gone to have fun with her friends,

00:32:45.225 --> 00:32:47.367
YANG NA KHYIS ZA BA'AM

00:32:47.367 --> 00:32:50.730
maybe a dog would come and eat me,

00:32:50.730 --> 00:32:53.936
which happens. Or

00:32:53.936 --> 00:32:56.494
YANG NA BYAS 'THOG

00:32:56.494 --> 00:32:58.435
YANG NA

00:32:58.435 --> 00:33:02.450
or else maybe I could be
carried away by a large bird.

00:33:02.450 --> 00:33:06.750
And I've seen small animals
carried away by birds

00:33:06.750 --> 00:33:10.830
in the desert. Baby animals
do get carried away by birds.

00:33:10.830 --> 00:33:12.510
It could happen to a human.

00:33:12.510 --> 00:33:16.450
There's a story of the first Dalai Lama.

00:33:16.450 --> 00:33:20.490
His parents' camp was attacked by bandits.

00:33:20.490 --> 00:33:24.360
His mom hid him in some rocks,

00:33:24.360 --> 00:33:27.240
and came back to fight.

00:33:27.240 --> 00:33:30.010
Then when they went to find him,

00:33:30.010 --> 00:33:35.010
he was being protected by
a large vulture or eagle.

00:33:37.003 --> 00:33:38.290
It was standing over him.

00:33:38.290 --> 00:33:43.290
Anyway, it could happen that
I was carried away by a bird.

00:33:43.636 --> 00:33:44.977
G-YANG DU LHUNG BA

00:33:44.977 --> 00:33:46.370
Or I could fall off a table

00:33:46.370 --> 00:33:49.420
or off a chair and break my head open.

00:33:49.420 --> 00:33:53.007
This G-YANG means fall into

00:33:53.007 --> 00:33:55.547
a canyon or some kind of cliff,

00:33:55.547 --> 00:33:57.618
fall of a cliff. Babies do that.

00:33:57.618 --> 00:34:02.618
SOGS KYIS 'CHI BAR 'GYUR BA LAS 'OS MED

00:34:02.725 --> 00:34:05.891
I would have died if she had abandoned me

00:34:05.891 --> 00:34:08.050
for even an hour or a day.

00:34:08.050 --> 00:34:11.291
I would have died.
Possible, I would have died.

00:34:11.291 --> 00:34:15.213
NYI MA RE RER YANG SROG
MGO BRGYA BRGYA BTON

00:34:15.213 --> 00:34:20.210
She saved our life hundreds
of times every day.

00:34:20.210 --> 00:34:22.610
And you can see it. I'm working

00:34:22.610 --> 00:34:25.200
with Seiji everyday on Zoom.

00:34:25.200 --> 00:34:28.330
He has a new baby, his wife Nour,

00:34:28.330 --> 00:34:32.125
by the way, they got married yesterday.

00:34:32.125 --> 00:34:35.355
They got their paperwork.

00:34:35.355 --> 00:34:40.033
She never, never, moms have this instinct

00:34:41.140 --> 00:34:45.200
not to be distracted for even
a moment from their child.

00:34:45.200 --> 00:34:47.610
She's totally linked in to the child.

00:34:47.610 --> 00:34:50.910
She's aware if there is anything
dangerous around the child.

00:34:50.910 --> 00:34:51.890
Slightly dangerous.

00:34:51.890 --> 00:34:55.800
And she's totally aware of
how's the child's security

00:34:55.800 --> 00:34:58.600
at any moment.

00:34:58.600 --> 00:34:59.980
If she hadn't been like that,

00:34:59.980 --> 00:35:02.610
we surely would have died.

00:35:02.610 --> 00:35:03.643
BU LA SDUG BSNGAL

00:35:03.643 --> 00:35:06.220
I have a close friend, close friend of

00:35:06.220 --> 00:35:10.210
my teacher who's child
was crushed by a truck

00:35:10.210 --> 00:35:15.210
because she looked away for
a moment. And it happens.

00:35:16.030 --> 00:35:20.709
They can't run. They can't
think. They just sit there.

00:35:20.709 --> 00:35:22.983
BU LA SDUG BSNGAL BYUNG BA LAS RANG LA

00:35:22.983 --> 00:35:24.816
SDUG BSNGAL BYUNG BA ZHE NAS

00:35:24.816 --> 00:35:29.816
If she had to make a choice
between my child suffers

00:35:29.990 --> 00:35:34.447
or I suffer, she would
always choose I suffer.

00:35:34.447 --> 00:35:36.833
This 'DAM means to choose.

00:35:37.690 --> 00:35:40.373
ZHING THA NA GNYID KYI TSE 'ANG

00:35:40.373 --> 00:35:42.290
THA NA means in the end,

00:35:42.290 --> 00:35:43.546
in the extreme.

00:35:43.546 --> 00:35:47.055
GNYID KYI TSE 'ANG
Even when she's asleep,

00:35:47.055 --> 00:35:49.700
part of her mind is still
looking at her child,

00:35:49.700 --> 00:35:52.883
still watching her
child, even in her sleep.

00:35:52.883 --> 00:35:55.458
SNGAR RGYUN LTAR GYI
LHOD BDEK NYAL MA PHOD

00:35:55.458 --> 00:35:56.800
She never sleeps

00:35:56.800 --> 00:36:00.730
as solidly as she used to,
before she had the baby.

00:36:00.730 --> 00:36:03.770
She never sleeps as soundly as she did

00:36:03.770 --> 00:36:05.210
before she had the baby.

00:36:05.210 --> 00:36:09.290
Her sleep is always half
sleep, because she's thinking

00:36:09.290 --> 00:36:12.230
is something happening to the baby.

00:36:12.230 --> 00:36:14.750
All right, and here we have a mother

00:36:15.650 --> 00:36:19.279
checking her child in the sleep.

00:36:19.279 --> 00:36:22.760
I think nowadays, even when we are,

00:36:22.760 --> 00:36:25.950
I'm going through this as a grandpa.

00:36:25.950 --> 00:36:28.648
I have a new grandkid, Maitri,

00:36:28.648 --> 00:36:32.977
and I can see that they've learned.

00:36:34.767 --> 00:36:36.792
Seiji and Nour have learned not to sleep.

00:36:36.792 --> 00:36:39.800
They've learned to sleep
halfway all the time.

00:36:39.800 --> 00:36:43.740
And it's interesting, and it's beautiful.

00:36:43.740 --> 00:36:46.710
So just think about the fact that your mom

00:36:46.710 --> 00:36:50.490
did this for you, and
that the ant crawling

00:36:50.490 --> 00:36:54.803
across the bathroom
floor did this for you.

00:36:54.803 --> 00:36:58.520
We'll continue with DRIN
DRAN in the next episode.

